# Project quality rules

## HTML and accessibility

- Use semantic HTML elements (`main`, `header`, `nav`, `section`, `form`, `button`).
- Every form control must have a visible label or an equivalent accessible name.
- Connect labels and controls with matching `htmlFor`/`id` when they are not
  nested.
- Provide visible `:focus-visible` styles and preserve keyboard navigation.
- Use `aria-live`, `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` for dynamic feedback
  and validation errors when appropriate.
- Keep heading order logical and use descriptive link and button text.
- Do not use a clickable `div` when a native button or link is appropriate.

## Mobile and PWA

- Design for narrow screens first and keep controls easy to tap, with a minimum
  target size of 44px where practical.
- Use responsive layouts without horizontal scrolling at common mobile widths.
- Use `inputMode`, suitable autocomplete values, and input types that match the
  expected data.
- Keep the manifest, icons, service worker and HTTPS installation flow working.
- Verify touch feedback, focus states, loading states and reduced-motion behavior.

## Feature completion

- Increment the Demo patch version for every feature.
- Run typecheck, lint, relevant tests and a production build before publishing.
- Do not commit `.env.local`, credentials or other secrets.
